From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: the menu doesn't pause a local wireless game

During a local wireless game (Emu::mp_active) opening the in-game menu no longer pauses the emulator: the
other players would otherwise stall or drop out of the race. While the menu is open the game gets neutral
input (no buttons, no touch), the frame behind the menu stays frozen, the game's sound plays at
kms.menu_live_volume (50%) and the header says RUNNING. Save, Load, Restart game and Cheats are off (and the
frontend refuses them while the game runs). If the session ends with the menu open (3 s without a local game,
so the wifi toggle between races doesn't count) the game pauses then and the menu becomes the normal one.
3D-effect changes made from the menu are handed to the emulator's thread. kms.menu_live=off keeps the old
pausing menu.
